  "reason": "RNA-only multiprofile with avgpool and PCA is currently the strongest setting, clearly outperforming singleprofile RNA and transformer aggregation, while image-only models are weak. The main remaining uncertainty is whether a learned RNA encoder can improve over PCA under the same profile and aggregation. config_005 tests only the RNA encoder by replacing pca_n2000 with scvi_n200 while keeping multiprofile and avgpool fixed, isolating the representation effect. This is the best next use of budget because it avoids changing multiple factors, reduces uncertainty about RNA representation, and will inform whether future multimodal experiments should build on a stronger RNA backbone."
